After the choice of airfoil, a pitch was found to keep the airfoil at various cross sections optimal in its wind velocity vector. This function was chosen to be $\theta(r) = r_0 - \tan^{-1}\!\left(\frac{4.8}{157.1}\, r\right)$ where theta is the pitch and r is the radius from the base of the blade. The numerical values come from the wind speed and RPM chosen. After structural validation in MATLAB, a 40% taper was necessary for the blade, and a 60% taper was chosen for a factor of safety of 1.5. With this, the final blade design was created. My main work included developing the code for the simulation of the wind turbine under various conditions.



